WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.989
"Ashwagandha, Ginseng, and Maca Root
for Female Sexual Dysfunction"

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.640
DHEA supplements
don’t seem to help

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.880
with female sexual dysfunction,

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:15.240
but what about
other dietary supplements,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:21.720
such as the three roots:
ginseng, maca, and ashwagandha?

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.320
Ginseng has been suggested,

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.480
given its demonstrated efficacy
for male erectile dysfunction

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.120
and the fact that it causes
a relaxation response in vitro

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:34.760
to isolated strips
of rabbit vaginal tissue.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.520
But when put to the test
in human studies,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:38.880
a meta-analysis found

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.640
no statistically significant
effect of ginseng

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.200
on female sexual dysfunction.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.280
Maca root has been advertised
as Peruvian Viagra.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.960
It’s an important dietary staple

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:51.880
of the indigenous people
of Peru

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.120
but appears
to have been overly hyped

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.400
as a libido enhancer

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.400
based largely on studies
of male rodents.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:01.320
Yes, maca seems to enhance
the sexual function

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.960
of male mice and rats,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.120
but of the two trials
on sexual desire in male humans,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.760
only one showed
a significant benefit,

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.920
but it took eight weeks
to show an effect,

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.440
which may explain
the negative results

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.920
of the second study,
which only lasted two weeks.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.560
A pilot study
without a placebo control

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.600
on the management
of sexual dysfunction

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.600
induced by SSRIs (due to drugs
like Prozac or Zoloft)

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:28.600
on mostly women
suggested maca may be useful,

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.120
but when properly put
to the test in a randomized,

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.400
double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial,

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.440
it failed to have
a significant effect.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.600
The necessity of placebos
is illustrated

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.320
by a maca trial
for infertility.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.880
Maca increased
sperm concentration

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:45.720
by 40 percent!

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.200
Yeah, but the placebo
in the study

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.320
improved sperm concentration
by 76 percent,

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.480
so maca didn’t work after all.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.320
Having placebo controls
is particularly important

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.840
for female sexual dysfunction,

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.320
since based on studies
of almost 4,000 women,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.960
the placebo effect accounts
for more than two-thirds

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.240
of the treatment effect,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.160
similar to the placebo efficacy
of antidepressants.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.600
In contrast, improvement rates
for erectile dysfunction

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.040
in men given placebos

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:20.160
are on the order
of 15 percent or less.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.400
The thought is that just the act
of consistent self-monitoring

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.440
in female sexual dysfunction
trials,

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.040
for example by being asked
to keep a symptom diary,

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:32.040
may improve symptoms
by heightening

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.880
the participant’s attention
and awareness

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.080
of her own responses
and behaviors,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.040
even in lieu
of an active treatment.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.360
There was one small randomized,
double-blind,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:42.840
placebo-controlled trial of maca

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.520
for sexual dysfunction
in postmenopausal women.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.440
Fourteen women
were randomized

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.640
to about 3/4 of a teaspoon
(~4 g) of maca powder

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.560
or a placebo powder
every day for six weeks,

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.520
after which point they switched
for another six weeks.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.880
While on the real maca,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.960
they reported
significantly fewer symptoms

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.480
of sexual dysfunction.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.840
Ashwagandha is a revered herb

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.480
of the traditional Indian
Ayurvedic system of medicine.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.160
Its name comes from "ashwa,"
which means horse,

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:13.400
and "gandha,"
which means smell,

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.080
because the roots
evidently possess

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.880
the "distinctive smell
of a wet horse."

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:22.320
Ashwagandha is used
as a household remedy in India

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.120
where it’s been considered
a rasayana, a "rejuvenator,"

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.320
or "tonic,"
for thousands of years,

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.600
earning it the nickname
of Indian ginseng.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.640
After being fed the root,

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.080
rodents thrown
into the deep end

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.000
swim twice as long
before sinking

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.680
(12 hours versus 6 hours).

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.400
Benefits for
physical performance

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.480
(including an increase
in aerobic fitness)

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.320
have been found in people too.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.360
One study demonstrated evidence
of cognitive benefits as well.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.400
Its Latin name,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.160
Withania somnifera
points to another use

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.480
(somnifera means
"sleep-inducer").

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.000
A meta-analysis of five
randomized controlled trials

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.320
of ashwagandha extracts

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.280
found a small
but significant effect

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.560
on overall sleep.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:11.000
What about ashwagandha
and female sexual dysfunction?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.840
Women ages 21 thorough 50
were randomized

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.840
to two months
of the estimated equivalent

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.520
of three grams
of ashwagandha root powder

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.720
and did not have
an increase in sexual desire,

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.960
but they did show improvements
over placebo in arousal,

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.920
lubrication, orgasm,
and satisfaction,

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.240
translating into an additional

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.280
quote-unquote
"successful sexual encounter"

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.520
by the end of the study.

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:36.080
What are the downsides?

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.920
Ashwagandha belongs
to the nightshade family,

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.080
which includes some
shady characters like tobacco

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.000
and, well,
deadly nightshade.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.080
There have been rare cases

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.320
of ashwagandha-linked
liver toxicity reported,

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:50.960
though commercial
herbal supplements

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:52.200
are often mislabeled,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.840
so it’s hard to definitively
attribute certain cases.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.160
However, there have been
several liver injury cases

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:00.280
in which the supplements
have been tested

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.000
and found to be
contaminant-free,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.680
suggesting that ashwagandha-
induced liver toxicity

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.880
is a real phenomenon,
however rare.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.400
What should we expect
from a plant

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:29.480
known by its other nickname,
poison gooseberry.

